Z||000000||trackerrrr||10-30-1999||10:39 PM||||Is there an easy way to remove the coolant pipes on my '84 Sport Coupe?  I spent three hours at the salvage yard trying to get the left one off a wrecked Fiero and still wasn't sucessful.  I had to remove the left front lower control arm, spring, and unbolt the steering rack just to get the thing to move and it still won't come out!  Does the car have to be raised with a lift to remove the pipes?||||reg||5
Z||000001||TOM||10-31-1999||01:23 AM||||Cut them in half and put them back together with a short piece of radiator hose and some clamps. I did this years ago and they are still leak free.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||10-31-1999||05:51 AM||||Tom<BR>That's too simple of an answer, working on a Fiero is supposed to be frustrating.||||reg||1
Z||000003||trackerrrr||11-02-1999||02:40 AM||||Thanks guys but I'm trying to get it off in one piece.  My original has already been cut in two because it rotted out from the inside.  The junkyard replacement looks brand new inside so I don't want to cut it.  So far Phil the only easy thing about working on my Fiero has been changing out side marker bulbs.  But I love it anyway.||||reg||1
